<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43641" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sĕnīlis</span></b> , e,
			adj.
		senex, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to old people</i>, <i>aged</i>, <i>senile</i> (freq. and
			class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tages puerili specie dicitur visus, sed senili
					fuisse prudentiā,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Div. 2, 23, 50</span></i>
			; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">partes (opp. viriles),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor. A.
					P. 176</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">senile aliquid (opp. adulescentis aliquid),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Sen. 11, 38</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">corpus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Sest. 22, 50</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">artus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					7, 250</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vultus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					ib. 8, 528</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">genae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					ib. 8, 210</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">guttur,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					Epod. 3, 2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ruga,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. F.
					5, 58</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">statua incurva,</span>”
				<i>of an old man</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Verr. 2, 2, 35, § 87</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">anni,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					7, 163</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">13, 66</span></i>; and <b>poet.</b>:
			hiems (as the last, latest  season of the year), <i><span class="en">id. ib. 15,
				212</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">animus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					10, 22</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">stultitia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Sen. 11, 36</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">auctoritas morum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint. 11, 1, 32</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">artes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac. A.
					3, 8</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">adoptio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 1, 7</span></i>
			
			<i>fin.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">senile illud facinus,</span>”
				<i>that wicked old woman</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 4, p. 148, 9</span></i>
			.—* <i>Adv.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sĕnīlĭter</span></b> , <i>after the manner of an old person</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tremere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint. 1, 11, 1</span></i>
			.</div>
